        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: FSC Star\n- Places: Starachowice, Central and Eastern Europe, Yemen\n- Organizations: Eastern Bloc, Soviet Union, Warsaw Pact, Yemen Army\n- Concepts: socialist states\n\nFacts:\n- FSC Star takes its name from the city of Starachowice, where the factory is located.\n- The Eastern Bloc was the group of socialist states in Central and Eastern Europe, generally consisting of the Soviet Union and the countries of the Warsaw Pact.\n- FSC Star was sold in various countries for many years, not only in the Eastern Bloc.\n- The Yemen Army used FSC Star vehicles as an example of the brand’s sales outside the Eastern Bloc.",
